+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` still reaches the caller as a rejection, and fires `onError` with the session and the thrown error — the same argument shape any other orchestrator failure gets ([validated by: hands a throwing beforeSession to onError and still rejects the caller with the same error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+- `afterSession` fires for that throw after `onError`, and sees a session the turn never touched — the provider was never called and no entry was committed — so a cleanup hook can tell a session that never started from one that finished ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession for a throwing beforeSession, with a turn that never started](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L73)).
+
